Vendored GoogleTest for Stimfit

Release: v1.18.0
Upstream: https://github.com/google/googletest
Release archive: https://github.com/google/googletest/archive/refs/tags/v1.18.0.tar.gz
Commit: 063de7e9578f82b369302001269680b4b1553359
Archive SHA-256: 6e3191c1455468b3fc35a417fb565c1c5071aee1b7e7f85e30cf48a98d37d8b5
License: BSD-3-Clause (upstream LICENSE is retained as COPYING)

The complete googletest/include and googletest/src directories and upstream
CONTRIBUTORS are copied verbatim from the release archive. GoogleMock, upstream
tests, samples, and build scripts are omitted. No local source patches are applied.

Stimfit builds src/gtest-all.cc and src/gtest_main.cc as one static library using
its own CMake configuration. This preserves the parent project's C++17 setting,
MSVC runtime selection, thread linkage, and macOS runtime policy. Building tests
requires no network download and no installed GoogleTest, Abseil, or RE2 package.

To update, replace the entire include/ and src/ trees from a tagged release,
refresh COPYING and CONTRIBUTORS, and update the release, commit, and archive
checksum above. Remove files absent from the new release; do not mix versions.
Validate the container and numeric test targets with STF_TEST_WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS
on Linux, Windows/MSVC, and macOS.
